> I think everyone has a mandatory Death By Choking to get out of their
> system before their first ascension.  One rule of thumb: if you're
> saited, it is a BAD idea to eat a dragon, since they give so much
> nutrition.  Amulets of magical breathing can help out here.

Quite true. There was a time when two out of the four characters I had
taken post-castle had died of choking. One of those had an almost
complete ascention kit; he lacked only speed boots.

You should almost never eat while satiated(unless you have an amulet of
magical breathing). You might make an exception for wrathes, or perhaps
a floating eye if you lose telepathy, but even then be careful. I have
passed up a wrathe when I am satiated. If you have recently recieved a
message telling you that you have a hard time getting something down,
you should not eat at all (without "oMB).

One final note: for me, it is easy to see something small and think I
cannot choke on it. You can. Both of my deaths by choking were on small
meals. Don't let the small size make you think it is safe.



